+-- Migration 174 - the Room's own agent-level default quiet hours for what
+-- the person's AI initiates (WS-R183, "RelationOS for the person").
+--
+-- Quiet hours today (migration 134, WS-R131) live ONE row per FOLLOWER
+-- (`vy_room_follower.timezone`/`quiet_from`/`quiet_to`) - a follower sets
+-- their own window, or inherits nothing at all. There has never been an
+-- AGENT-level default the Room's OWNER can set for every follower who has
+-- not set one of their own - WS-R183's own brief names this gap directly
+-- ("reuse the Room's own quiet-hours setting if it is per-agent; if it is
+-- per-follower only, add the agent-level default with the smallest
+-- change"). This migration is that smallest change: the identical column
+-- set migration 134 added to `vy_room_follower`, mirrored onto `vy_room`
+-- instead - same nullable, both-or-neither pair, same IANA-zone SHAPE
+-- check (not a real zone-database lookup, migration 134's own header on
+-- why a shape check is what this schema can afford), same reasoning.
+--
+-- `api/_quiet-hours.js`'s new `quietHoursOkForRoomDefaultSql` reads these
+-- three columns with the SAME wall-clock math and the SAME "NULL, never
+-- FALSE, when unset" contract `quietHoursOkForFollowerRowSql` already uses
+-- for the follower-level pair, so a future caller can `coalesce()` this
+-- room default in as a middle layer between a follower's own window and
+-- any narrower proxy - see that file's own header for exactly which
+-- senders consult it as of this workstream and which do not yet (honestly
+-- named there, not left implicit).
+--
+-- Idempotent, one statement per request (Neon SQL-over-HTTP), no DO
+-- blocks, no functions - 009's law, restated by every migration since.
+-- Both new columns are nullable and default to null, so an existing `vy_
+-- room` row is unaffected the moment this migration lands - migration
+-- 134's own precedent for the identical pair, restated on a different
+-- table. Written as `drop constraint if exists` then `add constraint` -
+-- migration 134's own reason: an unnamed multi-column CHECK cannot be
+-- re-added under a name Postgres would choose for it, so this migration
+-- names both explicitly, and a run interrupted between any two of these
+-- five statements is recovered by running this same file again, every
+-- earlier statement already a no-op.
+alter table vy_room add column if not exists timezone text;
+alter table vy_room add column if not exists quiet_from time;
+alter table vy_room add column if not exists quiet_to time;
+
+alter table vy_room drop constraint if exists vy_room_quiet_hours_pairing_check;
+alter table vy_room add constraint vy_room_quiet_hours_pairing_check
+  check ((quiet_from is null and quiet_to is null) or (quiet_from is not null and quiet_to is not null));
+
+alter table vy_room drop constraint if exists vy_room_timezone_shape_check;
+alter table vy_room add constraint vy_room_timezone_shape_check
+  check (timezone is null or timezone ~ '^[A-Za-z_]+(/[A-Za-z_+-]+)*$');
